1_ What happens internally when a Spring Boot application starts?

A) Spring Boot starts by initializing SpringApplication, then builds the environment by loading all configurations. 
It creates the ApplicationContext, performs auto-configuration based on dependencies, scans and registers beans, initializes them with dependency injection, 
starts the embedded server, refreshes the context, and finally signals that the application is ready.

